{
    "test_name": "MOB.355_Work_Form_Render",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.355_Work_Form_Render",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.355` A work order's **form renders** \u2014 the achievable half of what `MOB.134` was\ntrying to do.\n- **Covers `/work/:workStageId/form/:formId`**, the only entry in\n  `MOBILE_ROUTES.WORK.children` and previously the one route in mobile with no passing\n  test. Everything up to the typing always worked; only the WRITE was blocked.\n- **Deliberately does NOT fill anything.** Typed text never lands in these fields\n  (measured \u2014 `dd_tests_mobile/_archive/README.md`), and work forms are freely\n  customisable anyway, so the render is the durable thing to assert.\n- **Template-agnostic**: names no field, form or count. It asserts the shape the renderer\n  always produces \u2014 the route, `#apm-dv-tabpanel`, \u22651 `.ws-form-widget`, real inputs\n  inside those widgets, and the trailing `Progress` bar that proves the whole component\n  rendered rather than just its first child. Survives the fixture's form being edited or\n  swapped.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f `#apm-dv-tabpanel`, **not** `#senor-work-form` \u2014 `FormDetails.tsx:106` renders the\n  desktop form above 750px and chrome.tablet is above it (trap 18).\n- **READ-ONLY**, which is also why it can pass where `MOB.134` could not.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Work Orders",
            "read-only"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
        "config": {
            "assertions": [],
            "config_variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
                }
            ],
            "request": {
                "headers": {},
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{ MOBDEV }}"
            },
            "variables": [
